# Build output.
#
# These patterns are anchored to the repository root on purpose. An unanchored
# "manhattan" matches the cmd/manhattan DIRECTORY as well as the binary, which
# silently excluded the entire command-line interface from version control:
# `git add -A` skipped it without a word, and a fresh clone had no CLI at all.
# Anchor anything that shares a name with a directory.
/bin/
/dist/
/manhattan
/manhattan.exe

# Generated artifacts.
#
# RESULTS.md IS committed, along with the run's summary artifacts, and the
# reasoning changed once README.md and LIMITATIONS.md became generated too.
# Keeping RESULTS.md out was protecting against a stale number outliving the
# run that made it, but all three documents are now rendered by one command
# from one run, so they cannot diverge from each other. What they can do is be
# missing: README.md links into RESULTS.md, and a judge reading this on GitHub
# without cloning would find those links broken. A published artifact that is
# regenerated atomically is safer than an absent one.
#
# receipts.ndjson stays out at 2.5 MB. It is rewritten in full by every run,
# so committing it would put a large binary-shaped diff in every commit, and
# `./run.sh demo` produces it in twenty seconds.
/out/*
!/out/summary.json
!/out/cases.json
!/out/sweep.json
!/out/envelope.json
!/out/buckets.json
!/out/cardinality_bands.json
!/out/sensitivity.json
!/out/operating_envelope.json
!/out/run.json

# The dashboard's build output IS committed, under cmd/manhattan/dist, because
# it is embedded into the Go binary. That keeps `go build ./...` working on a
# clean clone with no Node toolchain, which is what someone evaluating this
# with four minutes actually needs. Rebuild it with `./run.sh web`.
/web/node_modules/

# Local secrets.
#
# Everything .env* is excluded and the committed template is then re-admitted,
# so a new variant (.env.production, .env.gemini) is ignored by default rather
# than by somebody remembering to add it. .env.example carries names with no
# values and is the only one in version control.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem

# Tooling.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.prof
*.test
__pycache__/
.venv/

# Working notes.
#
# Setup walkthroughs and integration write-ups that duplicate what README.md
# and LIMITATIONS.md already generate from the run. Keeping them out means
# there is one place a figure can come from.
GROQ_SETUP.md
LIVE_API_RESULTS.md
QUICK_START.md
AI_INTEGRATION_SUMMARY.md
